{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018EyWQcCShty7zyVHHsBPTR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each \"planned\" experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"median\" tier definition. Let me identify all planned experiments:\n\n1. exp-005 (DocRED confusability study) - planned\n2. exp-006 (Interaction effect 2x2) - planned\n3. exp-007 (Error taxonomy) - actually DONE, but the plan says \"planned\" while registry shows DONE. I'll skip this since it's done.\n4. exp-009 (SDGD-zero on MAVEN) - planned\n5. exp-010 (SDGD-cal on Few-NERD) - planned\n\n\n6. exp-011 (SDGD-cal on MAVEN) - planned\n7. exp-012 (Multi-model validation) - QUEUED\n8. exp-013 (Ablation: random batching) - planned\n9. exp-014 (Ablation: per-type splitting) - planned\n10. exp-015 (SCS validation) - planned\n\nI notice exp-007 has conflicting status information—the plan marks it as \"planned\" with a note about partial completion via reeval_text_match, but the registry shows it as DONE with a success conclusion. I'll treat it as completed and skip it.\n\nexp-012 is queued, so I should generate predictions for it. I also see exp-008 (SDGD v2) is currently in PREPARING status in the registry.\n\nLooking at the median tier results, LLaMA shows directional consistency but weaker performance with correlation values around 0.05-0.10 and p-values in the 0.01-0.05 range, while SDGD v2 appears marginal or negative. The paper's shifting toward an analysis-focused approach with SDGD serving as an informed negative result, and I'm tracking key metrics like the LLaMA pairwise correlation and p-value ranges along with confusion ratio extremes.\n\nNow I'm working through predictions for each planned experiment under the median scenario. For exp-005 with DocRED's 96 relation types, I'd expect the confusability signal to replicate directionally despite the added complexity of document-level reasoning, though it's marked as P1 and not critical to the core findings.\n\nThe interaction effect test in exp-006 should show mostly additive behavior with perhaps a slight super-additive trend that doesn't reach statistical significance. SDGD's negative results would likely extend to MAVEN in exp-009 due to the same merge amplification issue. For the calibration variants in exp-010 and exp-011, calibration might provide marginal improvements in confusability estimation but wouldn't overcome the fundamental merge amplification problem, so they'd still underperform single-pass approaches.\n\nThe LLaMA multi-model experiment is where things get interesting—it shows directional improvement but with a weaker signal around r=0.05-0.10 with marginal p-values. Random batching in exp-013 would likely perform similarly to SDGD, confirming that merge amplification rather than batch composition is the core issue. Per-type splitting would be the worst performer since maximizing recall while destroying precision amplifies the merge problem. The SCS validation should show moderate correlation with empirical confusion around r=0.3-0.5, which directionally validates the embedding proxy approach but reveals it's not a perfect predictor. I'm also noting that exp-008 SDGD v2 is currently being prepared. I need to include SDGD v2 in the output since it's referenced in the median tier definition, even though it's not explicitly listed as a separate plan entry. Now I'm constructing the YAML output with detailed rationales for each experiment.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20497,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20497},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84d9748a-c232-409c-a5b7-d